{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 1079,
    "dDurationMs": 3581,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Relativity - the idea that everything is relative,\nright?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 4660,
    "dDurationMs": 3750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Relative to your perspective, your upbringing,\nyour age, your place and orientation in space"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 8410,
    "dDurationMs": 1170,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and time?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 9580,
    "dDurationMs": 4630,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Except that plenty of things - in fact, perhaps\nmost things - aren't relative."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 14210,
    "dDurationMs": 4290,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For example, George Washington was the first\npresident of the United States, World War"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 18500,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I happened before the movie Star Wars was\nmade, this picture shows three apples, and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 22660,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so on."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 23660,
    "dDurationMs": 4340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It is true that certain things ARE relative\nto one's perspective - is the apple on your"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 28000,
    "dDurationMs": 6640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "left, or my right? - is 50°F hot or cold?\n- is a car fast or slow?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 34640,
    "dDurationMs": 1940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "big or small?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 36580,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- and that's precisely what makes these concepts\nless interesting to scientists."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 41940,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In physics (and in most science), anything\nthat changes if you change perspective can't"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 46020,
    "dDurationMs": 4450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "be a fundamental property of the universe\n- only things that are absolute are considered"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 50470,
    "dDurationMs": 1689,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "'physical' or 'real'."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 52159,
    "dDurationMs": 4751,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And for a long time, physicists thought that\ndistances in space and intervals of time were"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 56910,
    "dDurationMs": 2460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "absolute, fundamental properties in the universe."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 59370,
    "dDurationMs": 3910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The special theory of relativity first described\nby Albert Einstein was merely a statement"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 63280,
    "dDurationMs": 4820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the realization that we were wrong: distances\nin space and time are actually relative - they"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 68100,
    "dDurationMs": 2290,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "change depending on how fast you're moving."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 70390,
    "dDurationMs": 4410,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But more importantly, Einstein also described\nseveral quantities related to space and time"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 74800,
    "dDurationMs": 4670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which *are* absolute: the distance between\ntwo events in spacetime, the energy-momentum"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 79470,
    "dDurationMs": 2740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of an object, and of course, the speed of\nlight."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 82210,
    "dDurationMs": 4060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Similarly, the general theory of relativity\nwas essentially the recognition that in fact"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 86270,
    "dDurationMs": 5100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "neither the acceleration nor the gravitational\nforce experienced by an object are absolute"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 91370,
    "dDurationMs": 1090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "quantities."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 92460,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Accelerations can transform into gravitational\nfields (and vice versa), depending on your"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 96300,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "perspective and the path you take through\nspacetime."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 99020,
    "dDurationMs": 4360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The more fundamental absolute quantity is\nthe *curvature* of spacetime, which you can"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 103380,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "think of as a kind of \"underlying\" or \"absolute\"\ngravity."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 107100,
    "dDurationMs": 4570,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Special and General relativity, are, at their\ncore, not about what's relative - they're"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 111670,
    "dDurationMs": 2910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "about what's real irrespective of perspective."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 114580,
    "dDurationMs": 5220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If everything were relative, then there could\nbe no science, no laws, no justice - just"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 119800,
    "dDurationMs": 1340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "opinion."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 121140,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Science exists because it turns out there\n*are* absolutes in the universe - truths which"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 125060,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are the same regardless of your perspective."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 127580,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You might even say that science is simply\nabout finding the truths that will still be"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 131300,
    "dDurationMs": 25909,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "true if you remove "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 157209,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the scientist."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 158209,
    "dDurationMs": 2,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So... goodbye!"
    } ]
  } ]
}
